A("There are two independent leaks. Fitting the scaler on all records exposes the test distribution; final remediation duration occurs after intake and is unavailable at prediction time. Split before any learned transformation, put scaling/imputation/encoding inside a Pipeline fitted within training folds, and remove or replace future-derived features with intake-time observations. Redefine the target and prediction timestamp explicitly. Rerun model selection and final evaluation on a genuinely uncontaminated holdout. A Pipeline fixes the fit boundary, but cannot make a future feature valid. Version the corrected dataset and retract the earlier inflated score.","Removing only the scaler leak leaves the future-information leak intact.","What other columns could indirectly encode the future outcome?",["Two leakage mechanisms","Fold-local fit","Prediction-time contract","Fresh evaluation"]),
