A("On AWS: identity/IAM and workload roles, Bedrock for managed foundation-model APIs, SageMaker for custom training/registry/hosting where needed, EKS/Lambda for workers, API Gateway for admission, object/metadata storage, Secrets Manager/KMS and CloudWatch. On Azure: Entra/workload identity, Azure model services, Azure ML, AKS/Functions, API Management, Key Vault and monitoring. These are responsibility mappings, not identical products. Application code still enforces tenant/resource authorization, quotas, budgets, evidence validation, retry safety, retention and evaluation gates. Pick one primary cloud and verify current support/regions before implementation.","A managed AI service does not automatically implement your business authorization or safe agent tools.","Which permissions does the application worker have, and which user permissions must not be inherited?",["Service boundaries","User/workload identity","Application responsibilities","Provider limits"]),
