A("Authenticate the user, then authorize the requested tenant/resource from trusted identity and policy, not user-provided tenant_id. Apply checks at metadata/source APIs, retrieval candidate selection, post-fetch/context assembly, cache lookup/delivery, trace access and every tool operation. Use cache keys with principal/authorization context and source versions; avoid logging another tenant's raw data. Service roles may have broader infrastructure access, but the gateway must preserve end-user scope. Test guessed IDs, cross-tenant joins, stale permissions and active-run revocation. Encryption is necessary but does not fix an authorization bug.","Authenticated does not mean authorized for an arbitrary document ID.","How do you enforce the same authorization contract in batch jobs and synchronous requests?",["Trusted resource policy","Every data boundary","Cache/trace isolation","Negative cases"]),
