A("Start with an asynchronous job API: create immutable repo snapshot/job, query status/report, submit scoped approvals and cancel work. Store durable run state in a metadata DB; artifacts/evidence in object storage; queue ready work; execute in isolated short-lived workspaces. Python workers perform discovery, retrieval, transformation and validation via adapters, with Java fixture parity tests. Illustrative planning: 50 concurrent jobs at 3 calls/minute means 150 model calls/minute; at 4,000 total tokens/call, 600,000 tokens/minute before retries. Bound tenant fairness, call/token spend and wall time. Publish job/ingestion/provider SLOs, recovery objectives and exact-artifact approval. Measure time-to-validated-change and escaped regressions, not code churn.","500 applications is an inventory size, not enough information to determine throughput or storage.","What changes if model quota is one-third of your estimated peak requirement?",["Explicit requirements","Quantified assumptions","Durable isolated flow","Policy, recovery and outcomes"]),
